      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-31T19:52:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The protocol allows for more than 1 timestamp to be added back to back. For example: http://cs/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/common/motion_sense.c?l\u003d1023 inserts just a timestamp. After which we might get a call to motion_sense_fifo_stage_data which would add another timestamp and data. I didn\u0027t want to have to keep track of how far into the future we looked.",
      "parentUuid": "72684b67_caab3b29",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 291,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 292,
        "endChar": 12
