        "uuid": "0ec49c03_e7708e0b",
        "filename": "common/motion_sense.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 896,
      "author": {
        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-31T19:52:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mostly to avoid confusion and make sure that people that are familiar with the code base don\u0027t make bad assumptions. I didn\u0027t want someone that has already written code here to use add_data and assume things went well (since they wouldn\u0027t think to look for the commit_data call). With this change we get 2 things:\n1. It better reflects what we\u0027re doing. It\u0027s a bit like a repo. We stage data, commit it, then when the AP needs it we push it up stream.\n2. Users familiar with the code base that might have missed this CL and might use add_data will get a compile error and will be forced to read the new documentation on the stage variation.",
      "parentUuid": "a3d7c314_a3761644",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 896,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 896,
        "endChar": 32
